{"id":"federal-formula-grants","tier":"OFFICIAL","title":"HUD formula allocations and CDBG outlays in San Francisco","question":"What did HUD allocate for each program, and how much of each CDBG award has the federal government paid out?","finding":"HUD allocated $32,078,940 across four programs in FY2026. The FY2025 CDBG award was $18,798,493. Treasury reported $11,362,066.55 in cumulative outlays for that award when checked on November 27, 2026.","how":"HUD’s San Francisco, California grantee line (key 063228) supplies the four formula amounts except for FY2019, where the City’s final action plan lists annual allocations separately from program income and prior-year balances. All four FY2019 figures match federal award obligations. USAspending supplies the award obligation and cumulative outlay for each matched CDBG grant to the City and County. Amounts in the formula columns are rounded to the nearest dollar.","limits":"FY2020 shows HUD’s original announcement. The final San Francisco grants were $3,291 lower for CDBG and $1,076 lower for HOME. The City’s action plan and Treasury records agree on both final amounts. An allocation is an announced funding amount. An obligation is a federal award commitment. An outlay is a federal payment against that award and can occur in a later year. One-time COVID and HOME-ARP grants are excluded. Blank award fields indicate that a corresponding federal award record was unavailable in this review.","columns":[{"k":"year","t":"Federal fiscal year","type":"year"},{"k":"cdbg","t":"Community Development Block Grant","type":"usd"},{"k":"home","t":"HOME","type":"usd"},{"k":"esg","t":"Emergency Solutions Grants","type":"usd"},{"k":"hopwa","t":"Housing Opportunities for Persons With AIDS","type":"usd"},{"k":"total","t":"Four-program allocation","type":"usd"},{"k":"doc","t":"HUD source","type":"link"},{"k":"cdbgObligation","t":"CDBG award obligation","type":"usd"},{"k":"cdbgOutlay","t":"CDBG cumulative outlay","type":"usd"},{"k":"award"